      "message": "[error] Line 163: 🔴 Outgoing calls enable `rtcpMuxEnabled_` before negotiation is complete, and `getIceCompCountPerStream()` then reduces ICE to one component immediately. If the peer declines `a\u003drtcp-mux` in the answer, this offer path has already committed to 1-component ICE and no separate RTCP transport, which breaks fallback/interop with legacy peers. Keep two-component ICE until mux is actually negotiated (e.g., default `rtcpMuxEnabled_` to false for initial outgoing offer, then switch to true only after remote SDP confirms mux for all enabled media). Apply the same negotiated-state rule to re-INVITEs.",
